Aember Arena ports the shape of keyteki's declarative ability system (card
abilities bound to triggers, composable game actions, keyword handling, fight
and damage rules) and uses keyteki's card data as a source for derived ability
rows. No keyteki runtime or npm dependency is bundled: the model was rewritten
in TypeScript and the derived rows are plain data (DSL + text hash, no card
text).

Files derived from keyteki (AGPL-3.0, same license as this project):

  src/lib/abilities.ts            ability model ported from keyteki's Card.js,
                                  CardAbility.js, AbilityTargets and GameActions
  src/lib/vendored.ts             boot-time merge of the reviewed derived rows
  src/lib/generated/keyteki.json  ability rows approved from the converter queue
  src/lib/generated/approved.json ability rows approved from the harvest queue
  scripts/keyteki/*               AST parser, lambda library, lowering tables and
                                  the converter CLI used to generate those rows

Because the AGPL applies to network use (section 13), the running app links to
the corresponding source at Settings > About ("Source code (AGPL-3.0)").


2. Master Vault / KeyForge card data
------------------------------------

Deck and card data comes from the official Master Vault
(https://www.keyforgegame.com) at runtime, under the fan-content terms of the
game's rights holders. Card images are loaded from the Master Vault CDN and are
not redistributed by this repository. The two demo decks (src/lib/demoDeck*.ts)
embed card names and text for offline first-run play only.


